"id": "numbers",
"el": "Αριθμοί, ώρα, ημερομηνίες",
"title": "Numbers, time, dates and money",
"span": "A1–B1",
"blurb": "Cardinal numbers and the ones that agree (1, 3, 4, the hundreds, χίλιοι), ordinals, telling the time, dates and years, prices, ages, halves and percentages.",
"intro": [
{
"p": "Most Greek numbers never change. The exceptions are the ones you use most: **1, 3 and 4** (and any number ending in them, like 21, 33, 44), the **hundreds** from 200 to 900, and **1,000**. They agree in gender with the noun: **τρεις άντρες, τρεις γυναίκες, τρία παιδιά**."
},
{
"p": "Because **η ώρα** is feminine, clock times use feminine numbers: **στη μία, στις τρεις, στις τέσσερις**."
},
